1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,850
The Silk Road.

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:10,212
The Silk Road was not a single route but a network of trade arteries connecting China to the Mediterranean for over 1,500 years.

3
00:00:10,212 --> 00:00:18,712
Silk was merely one commodity among many; spices, glass, precious stones, and religious ideas all traveled these routes.

4
00:00:18,712 --> 00:00:25,650
Buddhism spread from India to China along the northern routes; Islam entered Central Asia via the same paths.

5
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:33,562
Few merchants traveled the entire length; goods passed through successive intermediaries, increasing in price at each exchange.

6
00:00:33,562 --> 00:00:39,612
The routes declined after the 15th century as maritime transport became cheaper and safer.

7
00:00:39,612 --> 00:00:50,275
The Silk Road exemplified premodern globalization, demonstrating how trade transmits not only goods but ideas, technologies, and beliefs across vast distances.

